{% extends "base.j2" %}
{% block title %}Verification — does the algorithm find known great views?{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<section class="hero">
  <h1>Does it actually work?</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The ranking was tested against {{ n_positive }} famous, widely-celebrated English viewpoints
    (it should rank them highly) and {{ n_negative }} adversarial negative controls &mdash; forested
    summits, flat fens, valley floors directly below famous viewpoints, plateau tops with altitude
    but no prospect (it should rank them low). Every positive's photo was visually checked against
    the target view type. Human judgements were used only to <em>test</em> the ranking, never to build it.
  </p>
  <p class="lede">
    <b>{{ pos_pass }}/{{ n_positive }}</b> famous viewpoints pass
    (top-25% nationally or top-10% of their region) &middot;
    <b>{{ neg_pass }}/{{ n_negative }}</b> negative controls pass (bottom half nationally).
  </p>
</section>

<h2>Famous viewpoints</h2>
<table class="rank">
  <tr><th>Viewpoint</th><th>Region</th><th class="num">Nat. %ile</th><th class="num">Reg. %ile</th><th>Photo check</th><th></th></tr>
  {% for r in positives %}
  <tr>
    <td>{% if r.photo_page %}<a href="{{ r.photo_page }}">{{ r.name }}</a>{% else %}{{ r.name }}{% endif %}</td>
    <td>{{ r.region }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ r.nat }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ r.reg }}</td>
    <td class="verdict">{{ r.photo }}</td>
    <td class="{{ 'pass' if r.passed else 'fail' }}">{{ 'PASS' if r.passed else 'fail' }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
<p class="note">
  Photo checks link to Geograph photographs (&copy; their photographers, CC&nbsp;BY-SA 2.0).
  "Fail" rows are discussed honestly in the <a href="methodology.html#limitations">limitations</a>:
  most are cliff lips finer than the 50 m terrain model, or viewpoints whose fame rests on
  accessibility and framing rather than raw geometry.
</p>

<h2>Negative controls</h2>
<table class="rank">
  <tr><th>Control</th><th>Why it must score low</th><th class="num">Nat. %ile</th><th></th></tr>
  {% for r in negatives %}
  <tr>
    <td>{{ r.name }}</td>
    <td class="verdict">{{ r.why }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ r.nat }}</td>
    <td class="{{ 'pass' if r.passed else 'fail' }}">{{ 'PASS' if r.passed else 'fail' }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% endblock %}
